    "real-ledger-arm-coverage"
  ],
  "why": "Before Protocol 10 stellar-core let a ChangeTrust with the native asset as its line through validation and threw while applying it, so the ledger holds the native arm of the trust-line asset union with a txINTERNAL_ERROR result and no operation results. Readers that assume a trust line always names a credit asset or a pool, or that expect operation results on every failed transaction, break on it.",
  "notes": "Chosen with the locate index of the full pubnet scan (token `T|arm|ChangeTrustAsset::ASSET_TYPE_NATIVE`): among the ledgers that hold the shape, the one with the smallest lake object. Header hash recomputed from the header and every transaction hash recomputed from its envelope at capture. `expect.values` are written by hand from the decoded sidecar; participants, state changes and movements are the reference extractor's output, checked against the sidecar.",
